{
	title: 'INSPECT files: Hal editors of uncommitted files',
	spec: 'INSPECT what "files" (also the lone word: INSPECT "files") lists files with the Hal session and call that last declared and changed each (bash modifies, EDIT), from every session\'s file_changes records (src/host/file-editors.ts, shared with plugin failure reports, task njq). scope "project" (default for files) covers the uncommitted files of the caller\'s Git root (git status, untracked included, ignored excluded); scope "all" adds Hal-recorded files outside that root that still exist, such as /tmp. scope "self" is an error for files. Each line gives the path (relative to the caller\'s cwd, absolute outside it) and every session that declared and changed it since its last commit (all records for never-committed files), newest first, each session once with its newest call: session ID, tab number and name when open, the call (t<n>) and the time in the caller\'s timezone. The newest says whether the file still matches its after-snapshot (current) or changed since through something Hal did not record; files with no record say so. No argument selects last versus all: the list is short and the last writer alone misattributes earlier uncommitted hunks. Purpose: an agent that finds uncommitted edits it did not make can name and contact their owner. Advisory activity, not ownership; /changes clear hides that session\'s earlier records. Cost: one scan of every session\'s cached change list per call, on demand only.',
